  "description": "EWAXIL02 crystallizes in the trigonal crystal system with space group P 3 1 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C6 H15 O9 Tb1,C12 H27 O9 S3 Tb1,2(C72 H120 Cr3 N3 O57 S3 Tb6),14.25(H2 O1),1.5(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb8 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Cr3 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Tb9 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb10 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Cr4 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Tb11 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb12 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Cr5 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Tb13 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb14 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Cr6 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 8 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.356-4.151 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.29-112.70°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C6H15O9Tb,C12H27O9S3Tb,2(C72H120Cr3N3O57S3Tb6),14.25(H2O),1.5(C2H3N). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
